{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And they turned and went up, etc.</b> The verse's saying <b>וַיִּפְנוּ</b> means that they turned from the path they were on, for before the mission began they were righteous, as it says ״כֻּלָּם אֲנָשִׁים״, and from the time they began to go on this mission they became wicked and turned from the path of reason. See what I have written on the verse ״וַיֵּלְכוּ וַיָּבֹאוּ״ (Numbers 13:26)." "<b>And they spied it out.</b> Meaning: not as Israel said to Moses, ״וְיַחְפְּרוּ לָנוּ״, but rather they spied it out to know what it is and what its people are, and they did not seek to know about the digging out of hidden treasures."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:18.332246703Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}